  "x-semantic-checks": [
    "Joint states preserve every original provider and criterion, with complete finite numeric axes and original IID/MCMC provenance/history. Criterionwise and weighted approximate inputs are unsupported.",
    "Every retained numeric tie is declared genuine. No rounding, epsilon, jitter or inferred precision repair is performed; rounded continuous output requires source review.",
    "Monte Carlo equality basis is structural_declared: criterion_classes supplies one named nonblank label for every entity in every criterion. Within-class values must agree exactly in every retained draw; observed cross-class coincidences never merge declarations.",
    "Exact finite-law basis is exact_finite_law: positive safe-integer masses sum exactly to a safe denominator, and class partitions are derived over all positive-mass states; a supplied partition must match.",
    "Declarations are checked for numerical consistency, not scientific truth, jointness, convergence or finite-sample/numerical certification. The legacy applied-0.1 domain remains separate."
  ]
}
